Priority: 2
Area: UX
Status: current
Depends on: preserve-mode-state-across-switches

Goal:
Remove the shell status message `Restored canvas workspace state after mode switch` and the equivalent PDF copy so mode changes stay visually quiet.

Context:
The user explicitly asked to get rid of this message. The underlying restore behavior is still desired; only the status-copy surface is unwanted noise.

Expected changes:

- remove or suppress the mode-switch restore status message
- keep actual restore behavior intact
- verify that real error or recovery messages still surface when needed

Acceptance criteria:

- Switching modes no longer emits the restore-status message in the shell.
- Mode switching still preserves workspace state as before.
- Real save/load/recovery failures are still visible.

Notes:

- Keep this a narrow copy-and-status-surface cleanup.
